t status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOMATA, JIN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOMATA JIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOMATA, JIN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An emergency reporting apparatus with a self-diagnostic function, which performs a self-diagnosis by repetitively transmitting and receiving among a plurality of antennas at predetermined time intervals a weak radio wave that cannot be received except through these antennas. When no weak radio wave is received as a result of an emergency such as failure or theft, the apparatus reports the emergency to an emergency report reception center.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce dispositif d'alerte, à fonction diagnostique autonome, exécute de lui-même un diagnostic en émettant et recevant, de manière répétitive, sur plusieurs antennes et à intervalles de temps déterminés, une onde radio faible qui ne peut être reçue que par l'intermédiaire de ces antennes. Lorsqu'aucune onde radio faible n'est reçue, par suite de circonstances exceptionnelles, comme une défaillance ou un vol, le dispositif donne l'alerte à un centre de réception d'alertes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. U